## 3. Concrete Issues & Fixes

### 3.1 General Security Hardening

| Issue | Fix | Code Example |
|-------|-----|--------------|
| No HTTP security headers | Add **helmet** middleware. | ```js\nconst helmet = require('helmet');\napp.use(helmet());\n``` |
| Unrestricted CORS | If you expose the API to browsers, set CORS policy. | ```js\nconst cors = require('cors');\napp.use(cors({ origin: 'https://trusted.com' }));\n``` |
| No rate limiting → brute‑force, DDoS | Add **express-rate-limit**. | ```js\nconst rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');\nconst limiter = rateLimit({ windowMs: 60 * 1000, max: 100 });\napp.use(limiter);\n``` |
| No HTTPS (in production) | Enforce SSL at reverse proxy or use `helmet.hsts()` (done in `helmet`). | ```js\napp.use(helmet.hsts({ maxAge: 63072000 }));\n``` |
| Logging | Add request & error logs for audit. | ```js\nconst morgan = require('morgan');\napp.use(morgan('combined'));\n``` |

### 3.2 Proper Input Validation

> In the current app there is *no* input that reaches a database or command line. If you add query parameters or POST data, **always validate**.

```js
const { body, validationResult } = require('express-validator');

app.post('/users', [
  body('name').isString().isLength({ min: 1, max: 50 }),
  body('email').isEmail(),
], (req, res) => {
  const errors = validationResult(req);
  if (!errors.isEmpty()) return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });
  // safe to insert into DB
});
```

### 3.3 Authentication & Authorization

> For public /data endpoints, use a token (JWT, OAuth2, API‑Key).  

```js
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
const auth = (req, res, next) => {
  const authHeader = req.headers.authorization;
  if (!authHeader) return res.sendStatus(401);
  const token = authHeader.split(' ')[1];
  jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET, (err, user) => {
    if (err) return res.sendStatus(403);
    req.user = user;
    next();
  });
};

// Protect the route
app.get('/users', auth, (req, res) => {
   // safe return the data
});
```

### 3.4 Error Handling & Logging

Add a central error handler that never leaks stack traces.

```js
// after all routes
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  console.error(err); // could be sent to a monitoring system
  res.status(err.status || 500).json({ error: 'Internal Server Error' });
});
```

### 3.5 Dependency Management

- Keep **express**, **helmet**, **cors**, **express-rate-limit**, **dotenv**, etc. up‑to‑date.
- Use a lock file (`package-lock.json`) and regularly run `npm audit` or `yarn audit`.

